<title>SWEDEN: Marieberg rises after suspension lifted.</title>
<headline>Marieberg rises after suspension lifted.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-11-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Swedish media group Tidnings AB Marieberg rose 11 crowns to 184 when trading resumed at 1345 GMT on the Stockholm bourse.</p>
<p>The shares were suspended on Thursday morning, pending an announcement from the company that it had divested a 50 percent stake in wholly-owned tableware subsidiary Duni.</p>
<p>Marieberg sold the stake to Scandinavian Equity Partners Ltd which was set up in 1994 by Investors AB and AEA Investors Inc of the U.S..</p>
<p>Separately, Marieberg reported a loss of eight million crowns after financial items for the first nine months of 1996, compared with a 362 million profit one year ago.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1017</p>
</text>
